# The built index is committed and parts of it are binary. Git's binary
# detection is a heuristic over the first few kilobytes. It happens to be
# correct for these files, but a corrupted embedding matrix would not announce
# itself -- it would return subtly wrong neighbours forever -- so the guess is
# replaced with a statement.
#
# The index JSON is data rather than source. Its bytes are compared against the
# manifest, so a checkout must not rewrite its line endings either.
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.pdf binary
artifacts/index/*.json -text
